{
  "_comment": [
    "The radiusd service definition.",
    "",
    "It has no Triggers value, so installing the package starts nothing: a",
    "machine authenticates Wi-Fi clients only once an administrator has",
    "configured it and started it (radius service start). Automatic startup",
    "is enabled separately by radius service boot on, or Start at Boot in",
    "the window, which adds a boot trigger here without starting it now.",
    "",
    "The service must be named radiusd and run as Identity Service: radiusd",
    "checks at startup that its token's user is radiusd's own service SID.",
    "authd makes that token, and verifies the passwords radiusd relays, so",
    "the service requires authd. RequiredPrivileges names everything it",
    "keeps: SeChangeNotifyPrivilege to traverse directories, and",
    "SeAuditPrivilege to write its events (radiusd.evman) and the kernel's",
    "audit of its access checks. radiusd-policy.reg grants both, and the",
    "authenticate capability, to radiusd's service SID alone.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): radiusd notifies once its status endpoint,",
    "/run/radiusd/control.sock, is listening, even while its configuration",
    "is invalid, so that the radius command can say what is wrong.",
    "RuntimeDirectories gives it /run/radiusd. Its state under",
    "/var/state/radius is made, with its descriptors, by radius config init",
    "and radius accounting init, which an administrator runs.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the radius package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\radiusd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/radiusd" },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "Service" },
        {
          "name": "RequiredPrivileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["SeChangeNotifyPrivilege", "SeAuditPrivilege"]
        },
        { "name": "Requires", "type": "multi", "data": ["authd"] },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["radiusd"] },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "RADIUS" },
        {
          "name": "Description",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Authenticates Wi-Fi clients for access points, with WPA-Enterprise"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
